    screen.Ambient_light.comment = Configure settings related to the lighting in shaded places
    option.AO_Strength.comment = Configure the strength of the ambient occlusion created by SSAO, GTAO, and SSRT. §bⓘ What is this?§r ambient occlusion is the small soft shadows in corners and such.
    option.GI_Strength.comment = Configure the strength of the global illumination created by SSRT. §bⓘ What is this?§r global illumination in this scenario specifically is the light bouncing off a surface and onto some other area.
    option.LONG_RANGE_SSRT.comment = Toggle long range screen-space raytracing. this will allow SSRT lighting to travel ALOT farther within the scene from where it bounces/casts shadows. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very high
    option.SKY_CONTRIBUTION_IN_SSRT.comment = Allow the SSRT to take the entire sky and fog into account to create high quality lighting for shaded areas. This may introduce more noise. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r medium

    option.ambientOcclusionLevel.comment = Configure the strength of the ambient occlusion from vanilla minecraft. §bⓘ What is this?§r This ambient occlusion is in minecraft even without shaders enabled.
    option.ambient_brightness.comment = Configure the brightnes of lighting in shaded places
    option.MIN_LIGHT_AMOUNT.comment = Configure the minimum amount of light that can be in shaded places.
    option.indirect_effect.comment = Toggle different types of effects to make lighting in shaded places higher quality. §aPERFORMANCE COSTS:§r. Vanilla AO: very low. SSAO: low to medium. HQ SSAO: medium. GTAO: medium to high. SSRT: high to very high - GI is slower

    screen.Ambient_Colors.comment = Configure the color of light in shaded areas.
    screen.Torch_Colors.comment = Configure the color of light from torches or other placed lightsources.

    option.LPV_SIZE.comment = Configures the size of the volume for colored lighting.
    option.LPV_SATURATION.comment = Configures how intense the color is for colored lighting.
    option.LPV_TINT_SATURATION.comment = Configures how intense the color is for colored lighting passing through translucent things like stained glass.
    option.LPV_NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment = Configure the amount surface normals will affect lighting direction.
    option.LPV_ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment = Allows entities to contribute to colored lighting.
    option.LPV_REDSTONE_LIGHTS.comment = Allows redstone blocks to contribute to colored lighting.
    option.LPV_COLORED_CANDLES.comment = Allows colored candles to emit matching colored lighting.
    option.LPV_NOSHADOW_HACK.comment = Fix for Iris 1.7.0 and lower! Allows floodfill to work in Nether & End, but disables entity & dropped item lights.
    option.LPV_VL_FOG_ILLUMINATION.comment = Allow the colored lighting to light up the air around it.
    option.LPV_VL_FOG_ILLUMINATION_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Configure the brightness of lit up fog.

