    screen.Post_Processing.comment = Configure settings for all post processing effects, from anti aliasing to tonemapping.
    screen.Tonemapping.comment = Configure settings related to color and tonemapping.
    screen.Exposure.comment = Configure settings related to the exposure.
    screen.DepthOfField.comment = Configure settings related to depth of field.
    screen.Purkinje_effect.comment = Configure settings related to the purkinje effect.
    option.SHARPENING_AMOUNT.comment = Configure the amount of contrast adapitive sharpening that is applied to the image. This can really bring out lost details from anti-aliasing or upscaling.
    option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment = Configure the amount of bloom that is applied to the image. §bⓘ What is this?§r Bloom is the soft glow on everything, to describe that something is bright or not.
    screen.TAA_OPTIONS.comment = Configure settings related to anti-aliasing.
    option.SCREENSHOT_MODE.comment = §aTHIS DOES NOT CHANGE GRAPHICS QUALITY IN ANY WAY§r. Toggle frame accumulation to get a low noise image. §bⓘ What is this?§r It stacks frames that happend onto the next frame that is generated, so it is like a long exposure photo.
    option.TAA.comment = Toggle temporal anti-aliasing. This removes all jagged edges on things, softens the image, and helps remove noise for many effects. This will cause ghosting or trailing because it uses past frames for extra information on the world. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r low
    option.BLEND_FACTOR.comment = Configure how much of frame history is used. high numbers means it relies less on frame history, so it may look flickery and noisy. low numbers rely more on frame history, so it may look less noisy, but more smudged with more trailing.
    option.TAA_UPSCALING.comment = Toggle temporal upscaling. This retains a good amount of quality from a lower resolution image when it upscales. so you can still have a high looking resolution compared to typical upsampling and still have better performance.
    option.SCALE_FACTOR.comment = Configure from what fraction of your resolution to upscale from - §abelow 0.50x is not recommend, it is only allowed for fun!§r

    screen.COLOR_GRADING.comment = Advanced color grading options
    option.LUMINANCE_CURVE.comment = Enable the tone curve. This is independent from color grading and is applied first.
    option.COLOR_GRADING_ENABLED.comment = Enable color grading. The RGB sliders will not affect the brightness. This is applied after the tone curve

    option.TAA_MODE.comment = §bStandard:§r has the best antialiasing ability - uses more jitter offsets, but needs more frame history (set blend factor lower), it will flicker more and have more motion artifacts. §bResponsive:§r has the worst antialiasing ability - uses fewer jitter offsets, needs less frame history (set blend factor higher), so it can have fewer motion artifacts. §bTemporal Upscaling:§r Render the shader at a lower window resolution, and then scale it back up to fit the screen for better performance - has MANY artifacts.
    option.MOTION_BLUR_AMOUNT.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This effect makes the entire screen blur in whatever direction you move the camera, or wherever you move within the world. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very low
    option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION_AMOUNT.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This effect makes the edges of the screen have a color shift of red and blue. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
    option.VIGNETTE_AMOUNT.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This effect makes the edges of the screen increasingly dark the closer to the edges it gets. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
    option.FILM_GRAIN_AMOUNT.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This adds a "graininess" or "static" to the screen. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
    
    option.WATER_ON_CAMERA_EFFECT_AMOUNT.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This is the effect that looks like water drops or a rush of water as you enter or exit the water. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
    option.ON_FIRE_DISTORT_EFFECT_AMOUNT.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This is the effect of heat distortion when you are on fire or swimming in lava. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low

    option.LOW_HEALTH_EFFECT_START.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This is the pulsing red color effect that happens when health is low. Configure what health level you need to be below for this screen effect to activate. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
    option.CRITICALLY_LOW_HEALTH_EFFECT_START.comment =§bⓘ What is this?§r This is the grayscale color effect that happens when health is REALLY low. Configure what health level you need to be below for this screen effect to activate. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low.
    option.MINOR_DAMAGE_TAKEN_EFFECT_START.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This is the flash of red color that happens when damage is taken.  Configure what amount of sudden health loss needs to be had for this screen effect to activate. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
    option.CRITICAL_DAMAGE_TAKEN_EFFECT_START.comment = §bⓘ What is this?§r This is the intense red colored trailing effect that happens when A LOT of damage is taken. Configure what amount of sudden health loss needs to be had for this screen effect to activate. §a⚠ PERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low

